;
; crash: UDH-new-static before UDH-init must crash, not return a bogus value
;
gcompile(nl `print(|\n|)')
gcompile(printl x `print(<x>) nl()')
; vcudh.cpp has no initialization guards. udh_new_static dereferences the
; null UDH at vcudh.cpp:148 (UDH->StaticPrivateKeyLength()), so this must
; die by SIGSEGV. The point of the test is that a call like this must fail
; LOUDLY -- if it ever returns a value instead, the caller has no way to
; tell a real key from rubbish, and this test turns red.
;
; There is deliberately no try(* catch): a catchable USER_BOMB would mean
; the crash is gone, which is also a failure.
;
; Note: a SIGSEGV'd interpreter writes no gcov data, so this script
; contributes no line coverage. It is a behaviour check, not a coverage
; source.
;
UDH-new-static(nil)
printl(THIS-SHOULD-NEVER-PRINT)
